      "id": 1,
      "text": "Deep Creek was originally called Smith's Creek when founded in 1665 in Norfolk County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/deep_creek_virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Deep Creek appeared around 1763 after a surveying mishap involving George Washington.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/deep_creek_virginia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Dismal Swamp Canal, which runs through Deep Creek, earned National Civil Engineering Landmark status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://alchetron.com/Deep-Creek%2C-Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the Civil War, Union troops camped in Deep Creek and practiced target shooting on local cypress trees, remnants still visible.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/deep_creek_virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Dismal Swamp Canal is part of the National Underground Railroad, offering a historic escape route for fleeing slaves.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://alchetron.com/Deep-Creek%2C-Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
